@g4s8 what do you prefer?
- that `Meta` exposes a `Headers headers()` method that exposes all the methods currently in `Meta` pertaining to headers
- that `Meta` exposes a `Header header(Header.HeaderTag tag)` method that exposes `asInt(int def)`, `asString(String def)`, `asInts`, etc

@ammaratef45 I'd create some custom Hamcrest matcher to verify `Meta` headers, e.g.:
```java
class MetaHasHeader extends TypeSafeMatcher<Meta>, PackageOutput {
  private final Header.HeaderTag tag;
  private final Matcher<String> matcher;

  public boolean matchesSafely(Meta meta) {
    return this.matcher.matches(meta.header(tag));
  }
 
  public void accept(Meta meta) {
    MatcherAssert.assertThat(meta, this);
  }
}
```
and use it in tests like:
```java
@Test
void someTest() {
  new FilePackage(rpm).accept(new MetaHasHeader(Header.HeaderTag, "value"));
}
```

maybe you can find some better solution, like split output and matcher or create output matcher.

